{
  "description": "Candidate-corpus validation cases read by both the Go (go/controlmapping/validate_test.go) and TypeScript (test/control-mapping.test.ts) tests, which is what keeps the two validators refusing the same documents. codes is the complete set of refusal codes the document must produce, empty for a document the contract accepts. A case carries either doc, a JSON value, or raw, the literal document text — raw is for documents no JSON value can express, such as malformed input or a number outside the range a 64-bit float can hold. Control ids in these cases are real ids taken from the upstream KICS candidate corpus, so a case that claims a revision mismatch reflects one that actually occurs.",
